{#- Feature: Hub shared-file code delivery (included in hub participant + supervisor) -#}
{#- Version: 2.0 -#}

Hub delivery rules (the shared file store is the team's deliverable; chat is for
coordination only):

- Contribute code through the shared hub files, not the chat. Use hub_upload_file to
  create or update a file (e.g. game.py, utils.py, test_game.py).
- ALWAYS call hub_read_file first when a file already exists, so you build on the
  current version instead of overwriting a teammate's work.
- Use hub_list_files to see what already exists, and hub_read_billboard to check the
  current project plan before deciding what to build.
- Do NOT paste full code files into chat messages. In chat, announce what file you
  created or changed and summarize the change in one or two sentences.
- Keep each file within the hub limit ({{ hub_max_file_bytes | default(32768) }} bytes);
  split large work across multiple files.
- When delegating to coding subagents, have them return the full file content so you can
  upload it with hub_upload_file.
